              "type": "text",
              "content": "For my father, books were knowledge. They were important to him. And yet he loved his children. What he did next was _39_. Instead of punishing my brother, he sat down, took the pen from my brother's hand, and then wrote in the book himself, alongside the scribbles John had made: \"40 work, 1959, age 2.\" How many times have I looked into your beautiful face and into your warm eyes looking up at"
